        "title": "bereavement-policy-v1.md",
        "text": "# Marsa Airways Bereavement Fare Policy\nVersion: 1.0\nEffective: 2022-03-01\nOwner: Customer Relations\n\n## 1 Purpose\nThis policy sets out how Marsa Airways supports customers who must travel because of the death of an immediate family member.\n\n## 2 Eligibility\nImmediate family means spouse, parent, child, sibling, grandparent or grandchild. The customer must be the person travelling.\n\n## 3 Fare\nA discount of up to 30% applies to the lowest available economy fare on the day of booking. The discount cannot be combined with promotional fares.\n\n## 4 Claims\n### 4.1 Documentation\nA death certificate, funeral notice or letter from the hospital must be provided within 14 days of booking.\n### 4.2 Retroactive claims\nA customer who travels before applying may submit a request for a bereavement refund within 90 days of the ticket issue date, and the difference between the fare paid and the bereavement fare will be refunded to the original form of payment.\n\n## 5 Contact\nRequests are handled by Customer Relations at care@marsa.example or through the Marsa app.\n",
        "highlight": "within 90 days of the ticket issue date"
      }
    },
